Chapter: DeckHoleEnterTest
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 CAN AN APP ENTER A HOLE? D.5 wants a desk pane to allocate inside a dead
 buried block instead of at the frontier, and the design says the way to do
 that is to ENTER the block, because outside an extent R10 is the bivy
 frontier and a ceiling armed on a hole would condemn every later
 allocation. What that costs was the open question: whether entering needs
 the compiler, or whether an ordinary program can do it.

 It can, and this arm is the evidence. `__deck-set` points the deck cursor,
 `__deck-enter` copies that cursor into R10 and arms the ceiling from
 `deck-reservation-top-cell`, and `__deck-exit` puts R10 back. All three are
 builtins, the cell is a fixed physical address, and nothing here cites the
 compiler. `build` in `Core/PhaseAllocator.codex` is the RESERVATION
 primitive and is not wanted: the block already exists.

 The first line is the control and it is what makes the third mean
 anything. An allocation taken before the extent must NOT land in the
 block, or the block would be where allocations were going anyway and
 entering would be proving nothing.

Section: Body

  dhe-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dhe-yn (v) = if v then "PASS" else "FAIL"

 Eight stores because poke-byte is the only poke primitive, the same shape
 `poke-qword-cell` has in the allocator.

  dhe-poke-q : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  dhe-poke-q (addr) (v) =
    let b0 = poke-byte addr 0 (int-mod v 256)
    in let b1 = poke-byte addr 1 (int-mod (v / 256) 256)
    in let b2 = poke-byte addr 2 (int-mod (v / 65536) 256)
    in let b3 = poke-byte addr 3 (int-mod (v / 16777216) 256)
    in let b4 = poke-byte addr 4 (int-mod (v / 4294967296) 256)
    in let b5 = poke-byte addr 5 (int-mod (v / 1099511627776) 256)
    in let b6 = poke-byte addr 6 (int-mod (v / 281474976710656) 256)
    in poke-byte addr 7 (int-mod (v / 72057594037927936) 256)

  dhe-reservation-top-cell : Integer = 36344

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let hole = alloc-bytes 4096
    in let top = hole + 4096
    in let outside = alloc-bytes 64
    in let f0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let w = dhe-poke-q dhe-reservation-top-cell top
    in let s = __deck-set hole
    in let en = __deck-enter
    in let inside = alloc-bytes 64
    in let ex = __deck-exit
    in let f1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in act
      print-line-uni ("CONTROL, an allocation before the extent is not in the block: " & dhe-yn (outside < hole | outside >= top))
      print-line-uni ("an allocation inside the extent comes from the block: " & dhe-yn (inside >= hole & inside < top))
      print-line-uni ("the frontier is unmoved by the extent: " & dhe-yn (f1 == f0))
      print-line-uni ("the program survived the extent")
    end
  end
